  "body": "**stacked on #1527 - review only the commits after 8d5cbe8b; merge #1527 first.**\n\n## What changed\n\nRoot cause: `State::route_post_options` (`crates/ui/src/state_setup_post_options.rs`) routed by `post_options_owner()` only - own-or-document, the pre-#1515 machine law. With two setups following the document's post options, an edit on Setup2's Post page wrote the DOCUMENT's options (`SetPostOptions`), which Setup1 also posts with: e.g. \"Skip pauses and homes\" on Setup2 silently dropped Setup1's optional stops and trips home (wrong posted G-code).\n\n- `crates/ui/src/state_setup_post_options.rs`: new `State::post_options_target` = the owner, else #1515's `shared_mount_target` (the active setup when the document has two or more setups). Every option arm (Skip pauses and homes, Output, Threading, End units) routes through it: with 2+ setups the edit becomes that setup's own options via the existing undoable `SetSetupPostOptions`; with no setups or one, the document's, unchanged.\n- `crates/ui/src/state_setup_mount.rs`: `shared_mount_target` made `pub(super)` (one rule for machine, post and post options).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_post_page.rs`: under the options' own/document radios the page says where an edit lands - \"A post option changed on this page is Setup2's own - no other setup changes.\" or \"... sets the document's post options - every setup without its own uses them.\" (`options_target_line`, matching #1527's `target_line`).\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1526-setup-own-post-options-edit.md`. Accepted consequence: Output and Threading are program-level, so changing Output on Setup2 alone now makes the whole-program post refuse by name (`program_problems`, \"post the setups one at a time\") instead of silently switching Setup1 too.\n\nMCP: the server has no post-options tool at all (nothing in `crates/app/src/mcp/` names `PostOptions`), so no MCP bleed; missing parity filed as #1534 (P5, `MCP:`).\n\n## How tested\n\nNew `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/setup_post_options_bleed.rs`:\n- `an_option_changed_on_setup2_leaves_setup1s_posted_options` - document skips pauses, Setup2 turns it off: Setup1's resolved options (`setup_post_options::of`) and the document's still skip, Setup2 reads its own change, status names Setup2; undo/redo walk both.\n- `output_and_options_on_setup2_never_reach_setup1` - Output and the generic `SetPostOptions` (End units) on Setup2; Setup1 and the document untouched; two undos restore.\n- `with_one_setup_an_option_still_sets_the_documents` - single setup unchanged.\n- `the_setup2_post_page_says_and_does_its_own_options` - real page: AccessKit label names Setup2's own; clicking \"Skip pauses and homes\" leaves Setup1 alone.\n- `the_only_setups_post_page_names_the_documents_options` - AccessKit label names the document's options.\n- Updated `setup_post_options::the_option_switches_land_on_the_active_setups_own_options`: its \"Setup1 active edits the document's\" step asserted the bleed; it now asserts Setup1's own.\n\nMutations (each reverted): routing back to `post_options_owner` -> 4 fail; target always the active setup (single setup binds own) -> 3 fail; page line always \"own\" -> 1 fails; page line removed -> 2 fail; `SetSetupPostOptions::invert` a no-op -> 3 undo pins fail.\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (includes #1527's commits): green - ui lib + 10 ui suites, 0.4 min. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot exercised: a GUI hand check; actual posted G-code with two setups' ops (pinned on the resolved options each setup posts with); release-lane pixel snapshots (no PNG changed; the setup Post page gains one text line, which may move a release-lane golden at the cut).\n\nFollow-ups: #1534 (MCP post options tool).\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0 (stack base #1527 branches from upstream/main fd2f4f30).\n\nChangelog: With two or more setups, a post option (skip pauses and homes, output, threading, end units) changed on one setup's Post page becomes that setup's own and no longer changes another setup's posted program; the page says where an edit lands (#1526)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1526\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
